+## Sales (schema 3)
+
+- Schema 2 migrates to schema 3 by adding an empty `sales` collection and
+  a `seq.sale` counter; existing records are preserved.
+- Each sale row has an id, ticket, soldAt (normalized UTC instant), dishId,
+  qty (positive whole portions), and the scaled ingredient quantities at import.
+- Existing tickets are skipped as a whole. All rows in a new ticket are imported
+  together, and each file commits atomically. Consumption uses `sale:<ticket>`.
+- Ingredient snapshots keep theoretical usage stable when recipes change.
